<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:ns3="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:db="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.0-subset Scilab" xml:id="caldiff" xml:lang="en">
    <refnamediv>
        <refname>caldiff</refname>
        <refpurpose>calendar successive differences</refpurpose>
    </refnamediv>
    <refsynopsisdiv>
        <title>Syntax</title>
        <synopsis>
            cal = caldiff(dt)
            cal = caldiff(dt, c)
            cal = caldiff(dt, c, dim)
        </synopsis>
    </refsynopsisdiv>
    <refsection role="arguments">
        <title>Arguments</title>
        <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>dt</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        An array of <link linkend="datetime">datetime</link> values.
                    </para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>c</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        A scalar string specifying the type of calendar difference to compute. The default value is
                        <literal>"default"</literal>.
                    </para>
                    <para>
                        The following values are accepted:
                    </para>
                    <itemizedlist>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>"default"</literal>: returns a <link linkend="calendarDuration">calendarDuration</link> containing
                                years, months, days, and time components.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>"Years"</literal>: returns complete calendar years.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>"Months"</literal>: returns complete calendar months.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>"Days"</literal>: returns complete days.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>"Time"</literal>: returns the elapsed time component as a <literal>calendarDuration</literal>.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                    </itemizedlist>
                    <para>
                        The value of <literal>c</literal> is case-insensitive.
                    </para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>dim</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        A scalar specifying the dimension along which successive differences are computed.
                    </para>
                    <para>
                        <literal>dim</literal> can be:
                    </para>
                    <itemizedlist>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>1</literal> or <literal>"r"</literal>: differences are computed along rows.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>

                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>2</literal> or <literal>"c"</literal>: differences are computed along columns.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>"*"</literal>: differences are computed using the linear ordering of <literal>dt</literal>.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                <literal>"m"</literal>: differences are computed along the first non singleton dimension of <literal>dt</literal> (for compatibility with Matlab).
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                    </itemizedlist>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>cal</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        An array containing successive calendar differences between values of <literal>dt</literal>.
                    </para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
        </variablelist>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Description</title>
        <para>
            <literal>caldiff</literal> computes successive differences between <literal>datetime</literal> values.
        </para>
        <para>
            By default, differences are returned as <literal>calendarDuration</literal> values containing calendar
            years, calendar months, days, and time components.
        </para>
        <para>
            For a vector <literal>dt</literal>, the successive differences are computed between consecutive values:
        </para>
        <programlisting role="no-scilab-exec"><![CDATA[
cal(1) = dt(2) - dt(1)
cal(2) = dt(3) - dt(2)
...
cal(n-1) = dt(n) - dt(n-1)
]]></programlisting>
        <para>
            The optional argument <literal>c</literal> can be used to select a
            specific component of the calendar difference.
        </para>
        <para>
            With <literal>c = "years"</literal>, only complete calendar years
            are returned. With <literal>c = "months"</literal>, the result is
            expressed in complete calendar months. With <literal>c = "days"</literal>, only complete days are returned.
            With <literal>c = "time"</literal>, the result contains only the
            elapsed time difference.
        </para>
        <para>
            When <literal>dim</literal> is specified, successive differences
            are computed along the selected dimension.
        </para>
        <para>
            When <literal>dim = "*"</literal>, the input is treated as a
            linear array and differences are computed between consecutive
            elements in linear order.
        </para>
        <para>
            Missing datetime values propagate to the corresponding output
            values.
        </para>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Examples</title>
        <para><emphasis role="bold">Successive calendar differences</emphasis></para>
        <para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2 4 7])
d = caldiff(dt)
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2 4 7])

 dt = [1x4 datetime]

   2024-01-01   2024-01-02   2024-01-04   2024-01-07

--> d = caldiff(dt)

 d = [1x3 calendarDuration]

    1d    2d    3d]]></screen>
</para>
<para><emphasis role="bold">Calendar year differences</emphasis></para>
<para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = [datetime(2020, 6, 15)
    datetime(2021, 6, 15)
    datetime(2023, 6, 15)]
d = caldiff(dt, "years")
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = [datetime(2020, 6, 15)
  >     datetime(2021, 6, 15)
  >     datetime(2023, 6, 15)]

 dt = [3x1 datetime]

   2020-06-15
   2021-06-15
   2023-06-15

--> d = caldiff(dt, "years")

 d = [2x1 calendarDuration]

    1y
    2y
]]></screen>
</para>
<para><emphasis role="bold">Calendar month differences</emphasis></para>
<para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = [datetime(2024, 1, 15)
    datetime(2024, 2, 15)
    datetime(2024, 5, 15)]
d = caldiff(dt, "months")
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = [datetime(2024, 1, 15)
  >     datetime(2024, 2, 15)
  >     datetime(2024, 5, 15)]

 dt = [3x1 datetime]

   2024-01-15
   2024-02-15
   2024-05-15

--> d = caldiff(dt, "months")

 d = [2x1 calendarDuration]

    1mo
    3mo
]]></screen>
</para>
<para><emphasis role="bold">Differences along the first dimension</emphasis></para>
<para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2 4; 10 20 40])
d = caldiff(dt, "days", 1)
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2 4; 10 20 40])

 dt = [2x3 datetime]

   2024-01-01   2024-01-02   2024-01-04
   2024-01-10   2024-01-20   2024-02-09

--> d = caldiff(dt, "days", 1)

 d = [1x3 calendarDuration]

    9d    18d    36d
]]></screen>
</para>
<para><emphasis role="bold">Differences along the second dimension</emphasis></para>
<para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2 4; 10 20 40])
d = caldiff(dt, "days", 2)
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2 4; 10 20 40])

 dt = [2x3 datetime]

   2024-01-01   2024-01-02   2024-01-04
   2024-01-10   2024-01-20   2024-02-09

--> d = caldiff(dt, "days", 2)

 d = [2x2 calendarDuration]

     1d     2d
    10d    20d
]]></screen>
</para>
<para><emphasis role="bold">Linear successive differences</emphasis></para>
<para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2; 4 7])

d = caldiff(dt, "days", "*")
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = datetime(2024, 1, [1 2; 4 7])

 dt = [2x2 datetime]

   2024-01-01   2024-01-02
   2024-01-04   2024-01-07

--> d = caldiff(dt, "days", "*")

 d = [1x3 calendarDuration]

    3d    -2d    5d
]]></screen>
</para>
<para><emphasis role="bold">End-of-month difference</emphasis></para>
<para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = [datetime(2024, 1, 31)
    datetime(2024, 2, 29)]

d = caldiff(dt)
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = [datetime(2024, 1, 31)
  >     datetime(2024, 2, 29)]

 dt = [2x1 datetime]

   2024-01-31
   2024-02-29

--> d = caldiff(dt)

 d = [calendarDuration]

    1mo
]]></screen>
</para>
<para><emphasis role="bold">Leap year</emphasis></para>
<para>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
dt = [datetime(2024, 2, 28)
    datetime(2024, 2, 29)
    datetime(2024, 3, 1)]

d = caldiff(dt)
]]></programlisting>
<screen><![CDATA[
--> dt = [datetime(2024, 2, 28)
  >     datetime(2024, 2, 29)
  >     datetime(2024, 3, 1)]

 dt = [3x1 datetime]

   2024-02-28
   2024-02-29
   2024-03-01

--> d = caldiff(dt)

 d = [2x1 calendarDuration]

    1d
    1d
]]></screen>
</para>
